      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Antipyretic analgesics account for more than 95 percent of the analgesic market. The most important agents of this group--salicylates, aniline derivatives such as acetaminophen, and nonacidic pyrazolones--have been used for almost 100 years. Nevertheless, their therapeutic mechanisms and the molecular causes of the most important side effects remain unclear. Several common theories are discussed and challenged."},
